---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const updated = '3 August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use — Wander"
  description="Terms of Use for the Wander app and website."
>
  <article class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-site prose-legal max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">1. Agreement</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            These Terms of Use (“Terms”) govern your access to and use of the Wander mobile application
            and the website at {site.url} (together, the “Service”), operated by Wander (“we”, “us”).
            By using the Service you agree to these Terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">2. The Service</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Wander lets you create animated map videos from travel routes. Features may change over time.
            Some features require a paid subscription (“Wander Pro”) purchased through the Apple App Store
            or Google Play Store and are subject to those stores’ terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">3. Accounts</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and for
            activity under your account. Provide accurate information and notify us of unauthorised use.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">4. Acceptable use</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You agree not to misuse the Service, including attempting to disrupt it, reverse engineer it
            except where permitted by law, or use it to infringe others’ rights. You retain ownership of
            content you create; you grant us a limited licence to host and process that content solely to
            provide the Service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">5. Subscriptions and billing</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Paid plans are billed by Apple or Google according to the plan you choose. Refunds and
            cancellations are handled under the applicable store’s policies. Free tier limits may change
            with notice in the app or on this site.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">6. Disclaimer</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The Service is provided “as is” without warranties of any kind to the fullest extent permitted
            by law. We do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free operation, or that exports will meet
            every platform’s requirements.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">7. Limitation of liability</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            To the maximum extent permitted by law, Wander will not be liable for indirect, incidental,
            special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of profits or data, arising from your
            use of the Service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">8. Changes</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may update these Terms from time to time. Continued use after changes take effect constitutes
            acceptance of the updated Terms. Material changes will be indicated by updating the date above.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">9. Contact</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Questions about these Terms: <a class="text-primary font-medium" href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
